[node name="Terrain" type="Node2D" parent="GameplayPlane"]

; ⚠ DOWN TO THE SEABED, NOT A SLAB OF SAND. The shore was a 240-deep box with nothing under it,
; so between its underside and the seabed there was an air pocket the width of the beach: a
; diver who swam under the sand left the water, fell to the bed and could not get back in.
; The land is solid to the bottom of the world now, and its seaward face is painted where
; this edge is (see the shelf rows in dagat_backdrop_2d.gd).
[node name="Shore" type="StaticBody2D" parent="GameplayPlane/Terrain"]
position = Vector2(400.0, 1260.0)

[node name="Shape" type="CollisionShape2D" parent="GameplayPlane/Terrain/Shore"]
shape = SubResource("Rect_Shore")

; 1709 + 120: the painted terraces rest their floor at plate-y 789, which is world 1709 with
; the floor dropped 360 under the waterline. The collision follows the picture, not the other
; way. It runs the whole level, under the land at both ends, so nothing falls past its edge.
